//! WebAssembly for one already-lowered MIR instance using demanded neutral layouts: the direct
//! backend's code generator, which needs no LLVM. Each definition is one `WasmObject.Fragment` of
//! finished function bodies and data objects, which `WasmLink` lays out as one module.
//!
//! # Details
//! The lowering follows `LlvmCode` construct by construct, so both backends give a program the
//! same layouts, calling convention, traps and failure reports, as an unoptimized LLVM build:
//! every function lists its frame name, a driver publishes its step records, and a switch tests
//! its cases in order. What only LLVM reads (attributes, lifetime markers, debug metadata, unwind
//! tables) has no counterpart. A construct the wasm body builder (`WasmBody`) cannot express yet
//! leaves the definition refused, and the link refuses the build with its reason.

